        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: stream control UI assistant deltas live",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nControl UI/WebChat and partial-reply preview surfaces consume assistant deltas from the live agent event bus. After the terminal delivery gate was added for embedded runs, assistant stream events were buffered behind the same gate as block replies, so live surfaces only saw the final assistant text after run completion instead of incremental deltas during the run.\n\n## Summary\n- Keep assistant stream delivery live for Control UI/WebChat and partial-reply preview surfaces.\n- Preserve the historical terminal-gated behavior for block-only reply delivery.\n- Propagate the stream-delivery intent through the embedded runner contract and subscription layer instead of only passing an undeclared call-site option.\n- Add subscription-boundary coverage showing assistant stream events can bypass the terminal gate while block replies still wait.\n\n## Evidence\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.before-terminal-delivery.test.ts` — 7 tests passed, including the new subscription-boundary regression for live assistant stream delivery.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/auto-reply/reply/agent-runner-execution.test.ts` — 237 tests passed for the auto-reply/live preview call-site behavior.\n- `git diff --check` — passed.\n- Live Control UI/WebChat proof is still pending; the code-level regression now covers the buffering layer that previously made the call-site-only patch a no-op and caused `check-test-types` TS2353.",
